Readers-Writers Problem Variations

- Reader-Preferred Solution: No reader is kept waiting unless a writer has permission to use the shared object. No reader should wait for other readers to finish simply because a writer is waiting.
- Writer-Preferred Solution: Once a writer is ready, it performs the write as soon as possible. If a writer is waiting to access the object, no new readers may start reading.
- Both variations may lead to starvation, necessitating further variations.
- The challenge is to find a starvation-free solution to the reader-writer problem.

No-Starvation Solution

Reader process do {
    wait(rd);
    wait(mutex);
    readcount++;
    if (readcount == 1)
        wait(wrt);
    signal(mutex);
    signal(rd);
    //reading is performed
    wait(mutex);
    readcount--;
    if (readcount == 0)
        signal(wrt);
    signal(mutex);
} while (TRUE);

Writer process do {
    wait(rd);
    wait(wrt);
    // writing is performed
    signal(wrt);
    signal(rd);
} while (TRUE);

